# Architecture

## Layout

```
/apps
  /app            # Expo universal client (web + iOS + Android)
  /api            # .NET 8 Web API — only process that talks to Postgres
/packages
  /shared-types   # TS types generated from API OpenAPI (NSwag)
/infra
  /docker         # Dockerfiles for api and app (web static)
  /migrations     # EF Core migrations (checked in; never edit applied ones)
/docs
  /adr            # One markdown file per architecture decision
  PRD.md          # Product requirements — read before structural/product changes
```

## Hard boundaries

- **API is the only thing that talks to the database.** Frontend never queries Postgres/Neon directly.
- **All new endpoints must appear in the OpenAPI document** exposed by the API. Shared TS types are generated from that document.
- **No breaking changes to shared-types without updating API and the Expo app in the same PR.**
- **No auth for MVP** (see `docs/adr/002-no-auth-mvp.md`).
- **One client codebase:** Expo in `apps/app` serves web (MVP hosting) and native later. Do not add a separate Vite/CRA web app. See `docs/adr/003-expo-universal-client.md`.
- **Placeholder product name is NewsFeed** (packages, titles, manifests). Find-and-replace when the real name is chosen — do not invent alternate brand names.
- **MVP UI is light with a single blue accent** (no multi-color brand palette / logo yet) so full branding can land later without a UI rebuild.

## Before structural changes

Read `.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc` and `docs/PRD.md`. Prefer an ADR under `docs/adr/` when changing hosting, auth, data ownership, or monorepo shape.
